Arktos Mobile changelog
=======================

Two-file convention: this file is the source of truth for release
notes; `app/src/main/assets/changelog.html` renders the same entries
inside the app (Settings → About → Changelog, or arktos://changelog).
When you add an entry here, mirror it in the HTML page.

1.0 — Arktos Mobile: first release
Rebrand / project:
- Rebranded the project from SmartCookieWeb to Arktos Mobile: package
  com.cookiegames.smartcookie → com.arktosbrowser.mobile, Arktos logo
  icon set in every density and flavor, dead hosted services replaced
  with neutral defaults (translate/news endpoints emptied, upstream
  suggestion + SearX endpoints removed), and every user-visible string,
  README, ONLINE doc and fastlane metadata now says Arktos (REBRAND01).
- Residual SmartCookie* identifiers renamed to ArktosCookie*
  (SmartCookieView → ArktosCookieView, SmartCookieWebClient →
  ArktosCookieWebClient, SmartCookieChromeClient →
  ArktosCookieChromeClient, SmartCookieViewTitle →
  ArktosCookieViewTitle); upstream project-name citations kept as
  attribution (RENAM01).
- Engine-coupling audit groundwork: engine/BrowserEngine.kt boundary
  sketch plus .devin/ENGINE.md + check-engine-audit.sh tracking every
  android.webkit touchpoint for a possible future selectable-engine
  effort (ENG01).
- LIMITATIONS.md documents the upstream issues that are Android
  WebView platform limits rather than fixable bugs (DOCS01).

Rust core:
- New rust/ workspace with an arktos-core cdylib exposed to Kotlin
  through UniFFI; Gradle cross-compiles per-ABI jniLibs via cargo-ndk
  and generates the Kotlin bindings at build time (RCORE01).
- BlocklistEngine in Rust unifies ad/malware/site-block/LAN verdicts —
  one call per shouldInterceptRequest; hosts-file parsing moved to
  Rust; public-page→private-network requests blocked behind a privacy
  toggle (BLOCK01).
- ArktosStore (rusqlite) replaces the five SQLiteOpenHelper databases
  behind unchanged repository interfaces; Netscape bookmark import
  uses a Rust HTML tokenizer (STORE01).
- Search suggestions, userscript metadata/@include parsing, download
  filename rules, bookmark JSON import/export and reader-mode
  extraction (dom_smoothie) all run in the Rust core; matching Kotlin
  models and helpers deleted (PORT01).
- URL utilities, error/block page builders, color math and the
  app-lock/parental password hashing (argon2id, in-place upgrade of
  legacy plaintext entries) ported to Rust in a second sweep (PORT02).
- Multi-list adblock subscriptions mirroring the desktop preset
  catalog, with per-list toggles, custom URL/file lists, staleness
  refresh and a privacy-settings screen managing them (LIST01,
  PREFS01).
- Tranco + Majestic site-rank lists merge a vendored seed with
  downloaded drop files through a streaming Rust parser, consent-gated
  behind the same privacy screen (RANK01).

Web-view fixes (upstream SmartCookieWeb issues):
- Error/interstitial pages got a stable non-null baseUrl
  (https://arktos-error.local) instead of loading with a null base
  under JavaScript enabled (upstream PR #329 for #328; FIXA02).
- StartPage search moved off the retired startpage.com/do/* endpoints
  to www.startpage.com/sp/search (#326; FIXA01).
- AMOLED theme: the active tab in the drawer now has a visible
  selection contrast against the black background (#298; FIXA03).
- The URL bar can trim protocol/www for display only — the loaded
  URL is untouched (#278; FIXA04).
- Certificate info dialog stays fully reachable at maximum system
  font/display scaling (#277; FIXA05).
- Text zoom ceiling raised to 400% while keeping the original
  25–200% steps and default (#275; FIXA06).
- New 'Follow system' theme option flips the browser theme and the
  dark-web addon with the system night mode; manual override still
  wins (#251; FIXA07).
- One-tap new-tab button in the toolbar while tabs live in the drawer
  (#299; FIXA08), plus an option to swap the tabs/bookmarks drawer
  icon positions (#297; FIXA09).
- Downloads verify completeness and retry truncated or retryable
  failures, resolve real filenames from Content-Disposition/mime type
  instead of falling back to .bin, and warn when a server returns HTML
  for a file download (#270/#311/#303; FIXB01).
- Error pages no longer persist their data: URI as the tab's URL —
  the original address survives restarts and undo-close (#281; FIXB02).
- First tapped link or pasted URL after returning to the app is no
  longer eaten by a mid-navigation user-agent rewrite (#309; FIXB03).
- SSL warnings are gated to one prompt per page load instead of a
  dialog loop that could freeze the app (#296; FIXB04).
- App links prefer installed handler apps over the Play Store, honour
  browser_fallback_url, and can no longer loop back into the browser
  itself (#316; FIXB05).
- target=_blank links no longer crash on undeliverable popup
  transports — the window request is declined and the link loads in
  the current tab (#306; FIXB06).
- A mistyped app-lock password keeps the prompt open with an error
  instead of killing the app (#302; FIXB07).
- Per-site JavaScript/cookie quick-toggles from the page menu and the
  long-press link dialog, overriding the global setting per origin
  (#305; FIXB09).
- A dedicated 'No internet connection' page replaces the generic
  error when the device is offline; reload retries the real URL
  (#323; FIXB10).
- Forced SafeSearch across Google/Bing/DuckDuckGo/Yandex behind the
  password-gated parental-control setting survives URL-bar edits,
  bookmarks and redirects (#327; FIXB11).
- Page translation rebuilt on a LibreTranslate-compatible endpoint
  (configurable, default libretranslate.de) with the wire format in
  Rust and an on-demand JS bridge — the dead Microsoft translator
  path is gone (#300; FIXB12).
- WebView hardening pass: intent-scheme allowlist on incoming VIEW
  intents, no user-CA trust, no cloud backup, download filename
  sanitization and dead-code removal (SECFIX).

UI:
- Error/block interstitials restyled to the Arktos desktop look —
  centered card, gradient header band, floated logo, hint list and
  pill buttons, emitted by the Rust page builders with an arktos-dark
  variant (UI01).
- Start and incognito pages restyled to the Arktos desktop startpage —
  aurora-wave hero, cresting logo and gradient header; the redundant
  in-page search box removed; customizable link tiles kept (UI02).
- In-app changelog page (this document) reachable from
  Settings → About → Changelog and via arktos://changelog; after an
  upgrade the changelog opens once in a new tab (CHLOG01).

Build / housekeeping:
- Build fixed for JDK 21 (jacoco bump, locale string fixes);
  jetifier dropped; dead dependencies replaced (BOOT01).
- Upstream housekeeping decisions recorded: own icon set (#168 N/A),
  GitHub Releases + in-repo fastlane metadata as the F-Droid
  prerequisite (#314), 'userscript' and manual-proxy support
  documented (#315/#325; HOUSE01).
